Someone recently asked whether magic protection would protect you
from involuntary teleportation.  The answer is yes.
It also "protects" from voluntary tele.   This tends to be bad.
Anyone who has played much on level 25 knows just how irritating not
being able to teleport (when you've been doing it against tough critters 
for quite a while) can be.  
There may be a few other, less than wonderful, effects of mag.prot.

Because of this, I usually use a wish on gray dragon scale mail and
avoid eating gray dragons.  You can take off the armor!
Unless you deity gives it to you (instead of feeding you when you are
about to die of starvation) I don't know of any other ways to get it.

Hope that answers the question!


